All files listed above were adapted for portable POSIX/gcc compilation:
MSVC-specific intrinsics (_rotl, _rotr, _rotr64, _byteswap_ulong,
_byteswap_uint64, __movsb, __stosb) were shimmed in msvc_compat.h, and
Windows-specific integer typedefs (unsigned long -> uint32_t,
unsigned __int64 -> uint64_t) were retyped for correct behavior on 64-bit
platforms, where the Windows types would otherwise not be 32-bit. No
cryptographic logic was altered; behavior was validated against the
official test vectors for each algorithm (AES, Twofish, Serpent, SHA-512,
PBKDF2) bundled in DiskCryptor's own crypto/tests/ directory.
